 "notes": [
  "H1/18 (2018 HY report p.12-18): pre-IFRS 16 as originally reported; no right-of-use assets/lease liabilities and no adjusted free cash flow APM (first published H1 2019). The 2019 HY report restated H1 2018 for IFRS 16 (full retrospective): restated ROI 996.2, op_inc 1048.9, fin_inc -17.9, pbt 1031.0, tax -335.1, NI 706.4, EPS 6.78/6.74, total assets 7520.0, operating cash flows 925.5, d_wc -37.6, adj FCF 681.3, equity parent 4753.3. Original figures kept here.",
  "H1/18 non-recurring: +52.7 net gain on sale of former Galleria store premises in Hong Kong (Note 8, p.22); allocated to Asia-Pacific in segment note.",
  "H1/18 CF uses the old layout: 'Change in net cash related to operating activities' (801.2) is after interest and income tax paid; 'Change in working capital requirements related to the activity' (-73.8) is not comparable with the later 'Change in working capital requirements'. No single 'Operating investments' line: purchases of intangibles (-27.0) + PP&E (-92.9) = 119.9 (= segment-note operating investments) kept in cf_other; capex left null. Key figures 'Investments (excluding financial investments)' = 128 (stored as apm.operating_investments).",
  "H1/18 CF FX is split into 'Foreign currency translation adjustment' 17.9 (cf.fx) and 'Change in foreign currency translation adjustment on intra-group transactions' 3.4 (cf_other); both needed to reconcile d_cash.",
  "H1/18 cf.da = 'Depreciation and amortisation' line 106.4 (excludes impairment 32.8, shown separately in cf_other). Note 7 shows impairment losses 32.9 (used for memo.impairment).",
  "H1/18 balance sheet prints no 'Equity attributable to owners of the parent' subtotal (total equity 4792.5 incl. NCI 3.5); key figures give 4,789. equity_parent left null.",
  "H1/18 restated net cash 2,798 is from key figures (integer); no reconciliation printed, so cash_inv_gt3m is null. Net cash = cash and cash equivalents 2,718.5 (Note 21 subtotal) less overdrafts 5.4.",
  "H1/19 (2019 HY report): first half under IFRS 16. CF splits D&A into 'Depreciation of assets' 111.0, 'Amortisation of right-of-use assets' 101.4 and 'Impairment losses' 26.4 (no single D&A line) -> cf.da / memo.da_cf null, components in memo.da_fixed/da_rou/impairment and cf_other. Same treatment for H1/20-H1/22.",
  "memo.da_fixed/da_rou are the totals 'included in operating expenses (Other income and expenses and Cost of sales)' = CF lines; the Other income & expenses note shows smaller amounts (e.g. H1/19 92.7 / 100.4) because part sits in cost of sales. D&A and impairment memo values are recorded as positive numbers.",
  "H1/19 restated net cash 3,740 from H1/19 key figures; the reconciliation (cash investments >3 months 208.2, total 3,739.8) is only printed as a comparative in the 2020 HY report (Note 3) - cash_inv_gt3m taken from there.",
  "H1/19, H1/20: 'Acquisitions of investment securities' kept in cf_other (in the 2021 report H1/20 comparatives this -8.6 was re-split into acquisitions of consolidated shares -4.3 and other financial assets -4.3).",
  "H1/20 (2020 HY report p.12): current liability line 264.9 is labelled 'Deferred tax liabilities' in the balance sheet but refers to Note 29 and is shown as 'Tax liabilities' in the 2021 report comparative -> mapped to cur_tax_liab (label error).",
  "H1/20: NCI line in IS is +1.4 (non-controlling interests bore a loss). Other income and expenses include a EUR 20m donation to AP-HP (Covid-19), within recurring operating income (Note 8). Covid-19 store closures: Q2 2020 revenue -41.5% at constant rates.",
  "H1/20: restated net cash 3,921.8 = net cash 3,741.8 + cash investments >3m 180.0; the definition deducting borrowings/financial liabilities only started with FY2020 (2021 report Note 3 footnote: H1 2020 financial liabilities were 8.7, not deducted). fin_liab_restated left null.",
  "H1/21 (2021 HY report): sector and geographic constant-currency growth taken from the H1 2021 press release (one decimal); the HY report rounds to whole %. Sector revenue values (1 decimal) also from the press release; report shows whole millions. Press release also gives growth vs H1 2019 at constant rates: total +32.8%.",
  "H1/21: CF 'Treasury share buybacks net of disposals' printed as '(158,5)' (comma typo) -> -158.5. The 2022 report comparative shows -159.",
  "H1/21: segment note footnote changed to 'Non-current assets other than deferred tax assets' (financial instruments now included); 'Holding' ROI -94.4 mapped to roi_unalloc.",
  "H1/22 (2022 HY report): all statements and notes printed in whole EUR millions (no decimals), so totals may differ by +/-1-2 from sum of components. Sector/geo constant-currency growth taken from H1 2022 press release (one decimal). 'Unallocated' ROI is only -4 vs -94 in H1/21 (allocation basis change; Note 3 says unallocated includes free share plan expenses and unallocated central costs and internal billings).",
  "H1/22: press release key figures show net cash 7,293 (equal to cash and cash equivalents) while the HY report shows net cash 7,280 (= 7,293 - overdrafts 14); report figure used.",
  "H1/22: 'Investment property' falls to 8 (75 at 30/06/2021) - presumably reclassified; no explanation extracted.",
  "Q2/yy quarter revenue and growth (constant / current rates) taken from the '2nd quarter' tables in the H1 results press releases.",
  "Headcount = workforce at period end (Employees note / key figures).",
  "Investment property (separate balance-sheet line in all periods) stored in bs_other."
 ]
